  "decisions": [
    "The game's pl0600_0 / pl0600_1 / pl0600_2 .mrl files share the same six materials and command structure but use different costume texture tables; pl0600_0.mrl is the default template.",
    "The vanilla pl_skin material 68b3d093 is the Stage 6 command template; its albedo slot is rebound and all other texture slots are left empty.",
    "Normal maps use 2266034a: source normal images are converted to per-material _NM BC3 textures, while materials without one share Null_NM.tex converted from assets/RE6/Null_NM.dds. The detail-normal and albedo-blend slots stay empty.",
    "Every base color image has its RGB multiplied by 0.6, a 40 percent brightness reduction, before BC1 encoding.",
    "Material output follows the reference mod: the .mrl contains only mod-specific albedo and normal materials, and the .mod may also list target-owned material hashes.",
    "pl0601.mod / pl0602.mod / pl0603.mod and event/face/pl0600/cs_pl0600*.mod are exported untouched.",
    "Target is locked to slot pl0600 (Ada) with a single body part.",
    "Stage 9 sets normal meshes to IASkinTB4wt and face meshes to IASkinTB1wt; the face material group is taken from the Stage 1 face-normal mask unless settings.export.face_material_names overrides it."
  ]
